The ‘imperceptibility’ of carbon emissions weakens the willingness of the public to act on urban carbon reduction. Wenlei Zhu proposes visualizing urban decarbonization by using bioreactive façades with photosynthetic organisms, to make carbon sequestration visible and perceptible.

